REALROM sample.note a034 [NesBankingAnalyzer] Bank value is RESTORED here, not resolved: this call's helper FUN_aa39 is a restore stub -- it loads the bank from 000e, a writable RAM cell, and branches to the helper's switch when it is nonzero (when it is zero the switch is skipped and the bank is left as it was). The bank after this call is therefore whatever was last saved at 000e, or unchanged -- a property of the game, not a gap in analysis.
